# Follow ZAP code organization

Put new code where similar code already lives. Do not invent a new layer or dump logic into the nearest open file.

## Backend (`src-electron/`)

| Concern | Put it in |
|---|---|
| SQL / DB reads & writes | `db/query-*.js` (domain-specific file, e.g. endpoints → `query-endpoint.js`) |
| Row → JS object mapping | `db/db-mapping.js` |
| HTTP route handlers | `rest/*.js` |
| Studio / IDE integration | `ide-integration/` (orchestration only; call query/util helpers) |
| Generation / templates | `generator/` |
| ZCL loading | `zcl/` |
| Shared non-UI helpers | `util/` |
| Import(open) / export(save) | `importexport/` |

## Frontend (`src/`)

| Concern | Put it in |
|---|---|
| Vue components | `components/` |
| Vuex state / actions / mutations | `store/zap/` |
| Shared UI helpers / mixins | `util/` |
| Pages / layouts | `pages/`, `layouts/` |

## Conventions

- Keep `require` / `import` at the top of the file (see `js-requires-at-top`).
- Export new query helpers from the existing `query-*.js` module rather than creating one-off DB access in callers.
- Tests that mirror a feature go under `test/` next to similar existing tests; reuse `test-util` and existing fixtures when possible.
- Match local naming, async/Promise style, and comment density of the surrounding file—do not introduce a new style.

When unsure where something belongs, find one existing feature that does the same kind of work and follow that file layout.
